  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform rod of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is hinged at its upper end as shown in the figure. A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;which is&nbsp;moving horizontally, strikes the rod elastically at its midpoint. If the particle comes to rest after collision, then the value of <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image24-2b929b41-1e15-4d77-ab62-31c1194635a5.jpg\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 203px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "0.75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Conserving angular Momentum about the hinge, just before and after the collision&nbsp;<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>ω</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi><mi>L</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></math></p>",
